# OkVevo-Nia is the only push target

**HARD RULE.** This fork’s canonical GitHub remote is:

- **Allowed:** `https://github.com/Jaikarans2003/OkVevo-Nia.git`
- **Forbidden:** `https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent.git`

## Git remotes (this machine)

| Remote   | URL                                              | Use                          |
|----------|--------------------------------------------------|------------------------------|
| `okvevo` | `Jaikarans2003/OkVevo-Nia.git`                   | **Only** remote for push     |
| `origin` | `NousResearch/hermes-agent.git`                  | Fetch/reference only — **never push** |

## Agent / CI must

- Commit and push with `git push okvevo HEAD` (or `okvevo main`) — never `git push origin`.
- Never set upstream to `origin`, never `git push --set-upstream origin …`.
- Never open PRs against `NousResearch/hermes-agent` from OkVevo product work unless Karan explicitly asks.
- If `okvevo` is missing: `git remote add okvevo https://github.com/Jaikarans2003/OkVevo-Nia.git` then push there.
- If unsure which remote a push would hit: run `git remote -v` and `git status -sb` first and stop if the push target is Nous.

## Do not

- Push, force-push, or mirror this tree to Nous Research.
- “Sync back” Nia/OkVevo commits to upstream Hermes without an explicit user request naming that repo.
